==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Miasma Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Bubble Cat''' when obtained from [[With Sympathy (Merciless)]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
While this unit seems promising on paper, his DPS is absolutely horrendous and cannot be used as a generalist. Even within his niche, he faces competition against [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] and [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]], as he struggles to damage Angel midrangers and the nasty melee pushers can quickly invade his blindspot, meaning his immunities aren't of much use either. Although he can barely outrange [[Winged Pigge]]'s Omni Strike (360>340), his DPS again holds it back from actually becoming a viable counter.

==='''True Form'''===
Bubble Cat's most significant gain is a large damage boost that nearly triples his DPS against its targeted traits, reaching a whopping 13k at level 50. This, combined with his impressive LD maximum range of 500, greatly increases his consistency against the likes of [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[Chickful A]], both of which are notoriously tanky Angel midrangers. Likewise, he also becomes a much stronger answer to Winged Pigge and can tear through her health quickly. Curse Immunity doesn't matter much, as most Relic enemies 1-shot him anyways, but it makes him really useful against [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]], like in [[The Prince's Woods]], [[Guild of Masks|Guild Of Masks]] and [[Darkened House]].

Apart from that, his new Floating target allows it to further differentiate himself from Mushroom Cat and Cafeteria Cat by engaging clusters of Floating threats from afar. While [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] is often the anti-Floating mainstay, Bubble Cat's range advantage hits further with great effect, being essentially a better [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] at that regard.
Despite the HP increase this [[True Form]] provides, Bubble Cat is still incredibly fragile for an LD attacker, especially compared to other units such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], and will still perish as soon as something enters his blindspot. Fortunately, he does benefit from his recharge time reduction, low cost and longer backswing (0.67s to 1.33s), allowing large stacks of them to be accumulated for greater destruction.
